1
00:04:53,684 --> 00:04:59,684
Raiders!: The Story of the Greatest Fan Film Ever Made is a
documentary film directed by Jeremy Coon.

2
00:09:47,368 --> 00:09:53,368
In 1982, three 11 year-olds in Mississippi set out to remake
their favorite film: Raiders of the Lost Ark.

3
00:14:41,052 --> 00:14:47,052
It took seven turbulent years that tested the limits of their
friendship and nearly burned down their mother's house.

4
00:19:34,736 --> 00:19:40,736
By the end, they had completed every scene except one...

5
00:24:28,421 --> 00:24:34,421
the explosive airplane scene.

6
00:29:22,105 --> 00:29:28,105
30 years later, they attempt to finally realize their childhood dream by building a replica of the 75
foot "Flying Wing" plane from Raiders in a mud pit in the backwoods of Mississippi...

7
00:34:15,789 --> 00:34:21,789
and then blow it up!

8
00:39:09,473 --> 00:39:15,473
This is the story behind the making of what is known
as "the greatest fan film ever made."

9
00:44:03,157 --> 00:44:09,157
Self, played by John Rhys-Davies.

10
00:48:56,842 --> 00:49:02,842
Self, played by Eli Roth.

11
00:53:50,526 --> 00:53:56,526
Self, played by Eric Zala.

12
00:58:44,210 --> 00:58:50,210
Self, played by Chris Strompolos.

13
01:03:37,894 --> 01:03:43,894
Self, played by Jayson Lamb.

14
01:08:31,578 --> 01:08:37,578
Self, played by Kurt Zala.

15
01:13:25,263 --> 01:13:31,263
Raiders!: The Story of the Greatest Fan Film Ever Made is a 2015 American
documentary film directed by Jeremy Coon and Tim Skousen.

16
01:18:18,947 --> 01:18:24,947
The film follows three childhood friends, Eric Zala, Chris Strompolos, and Jayson Lamb, from
1982 to 1989 as they set out to make a fan film of Raiders of the Lost Ark.

17
01:23:12,631 --> 01:23:18,631
35 years later in 2014, it shows how they get back together to finish filming the
"plane sequence", a previously missing scene from their remake.

18
01:28:06,315 --> 01:28:12,315
The film explores themes of pop culture, fan
culture, filmmaking, fan film, fandom.
